jellyfin-wake-hdd (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep the timer running across package upgrades. Previously it was
    stopped on upgrade and not restarted until the next reboot.
  * Install /etc/jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf with mode 0600 as it contains the
    Jellyfin API key.
  * Fix the README's default timer interval (15s, not 30s).

 -- Liam Newmarch <liamnewmarch@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

jellyfin-wake-hdd (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Poll Jellyfin's /Sessions API and wake the drives behind WAKE_PATHS
    when at least MIN_SESSIONS clients are connected.
  * Wake drives by reading one 4 KiB block from the block device behind
    each path using O_DIRECT, which always reaches the disk. A plain stat
    is answered from the kernel's inode cache and never wakes a sleeping
    drive.

 -- Liam Newmarch <liamnewmarch@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0000
